fjord is a web UI for managing container "compose" stacks on FreeBSD. It reads
compose files directly from the filesystem (no vendor lock-in), drives podman
(or appjail) to run them, and includes a daemonless app store for one-click
installs.

The daemon (fjordd) serves the UI and talks to the container engine. A System
page runs host-readiness checks (missing tools, dead podman socket, pf rules)
with copyable fixes.
